    "mixed nulls",
    "arbitrary random networks",
    "nonuniform feature-independent predictors",
    "population generalization",
    "regression confidence",
    "adaptive selected retries",
    "new attempt families without disclosed error accounting"
  ],
  "regression_reasoning": "Exact rationals of finite binary64 targets/predictions compute SST around exact target mean and final/initial SSE. Positive finite training-fitted scale cancels from strict SSE_final<SST and SSE_final<SSE_initial. Equality is failure; empty/misaligned/nonfinite inputs and nonpositive variance fail. This is descriptive held-out skill/improvement, not probability confidence.",
